Hi.

On Mon, Mar 8, 2010 at 6:23 PM, seth redmond
<seth.r...@imperial.ac.uk> wrote:
> I've been following the CRMAv2 vignette without any trouble, but when I try
> to reload the monocell CDF I get a file with multiple values for each unit.
> Is this normal? and how can I reduce it to one again?

Yes, it is normal, because a monocell CDF contains one cell per *unit
group*.  There are often multiple groups per unit.  Thus, a monocell
CDF contains multiple cells per unit.

In your case you are using a SNP chip - a SNP interrogates two
alleles, but may also interrogate the sense and the antisense strand,
and each of these are stored in a separate group.  Hense a SNP unit
may contain either 2 or 2*2=4 unit groups.  This is close to the
average number of cells per SNP that you have.

The above is also the reason why the term "probeset" is ambiguous; a
probeset is often a "unit group" whereas it is often the case people
use "probeset" to refer to a unit.  Because of this, we never use the
term "probeset", but instead "units" and "unit groups".

I don't understand what you mean by "how can I reduce it to one
again?".  More importantly, is there a problem?  What are you trying
to do that doesn't work?

/Henrik

